{
 "id": "bigville_coll_collect",
 "version": "1.0.0",
 "depends_on": [],
 "self_load_only": true,
 "description": "BIGVILLE R16 (block 264000) -- COLLECTION IS AN ACT (de-magicalizes R7's auto-debit). Rent transfers ONLY when a collector REACHES the payer (R1 proximity: collector and tenant is_at the SAME MoveCell) and acts. bc_collect_self: a small owner collects his own rent free (tenant.coin-=rent, ll.coin+=rent). bc_collect_hired: a paid agent collects into his OWN hands (collected/stated_collected buckets), delivery is separate. bc_collect_miss: collector reaches an insolvent tenant -> arrears++ (DISJOINT on coin<rent; covers both). bc_deliver: the hired collector delivers delivered=IDiv(collected*deliver_bp+5000,10000) to the owner and POCKETS the skim into his own coin -- an honest deliver_bp=10000 gives held_delivered==stated_collected, a saboteur leaves held<stated (the 234 stated!=held atom, on collection). bc_pay_wage: the owner pays the hired collector a wage (R4/R6), so the owner NETS rent-wage and the collector's take is wage+skim. If the collector is not proximate NO rule fires -> no transfer at all (failed to find the payer). Every decision a RULE; composes existing Terms; zero new Rust.",
